# ext/stage-receipts.json must never merge quietly.
#
# It is a set of claims about ONE shared mutable file on disk (the stage
# image every Mirror sweep clones). Two branches can each append an honest
# receipt and git will combine them without complaint — producing a file
# whose LAST bake entry, which every gate reads as "the newest bake", is
# whichever line sorted last rather than whichever bake happened last.
#
# The driver body lives in per-clone git config (tools/setup-hooks writes
# it), so a clone that has not run setup-hooks gets git's ordinary text
# merge instead. That is the reason .githooks/pre-merge-commit re-checks
# the result: an enforcement that lives only in a config a contributor may
# not have is a rule again, not a gate.
ext/stage-receipts.json merge=nowreceipts
